SuperEmbedding research implementation, 2026.

This project uses Qwen3.5-0.8B (Qwen/Alibaba Cloud, Apache-2.0) and
OmniJev-0.8B v1.1 (tinnel123, Apache-2.0). Published embedding checkpoints
with copied decision-gate parameters and fine-tuned LoRA adapters are
derived from these works. Their original notices/licenses are retained
in the model release. Inherited decision heads are not validated after
embedding fine-tuning.

FLAIR (Xiao et al., CVPR 2025; ExplainableML) is used as an external
baseline from its pinned official repository and MIT-licensed public
model card. Its code and original checkpoint are downloaded separately.

Fashion Product Images Small: Param Aggarwal / Myntra product catalog,
mirrored by ashraq on Hugging Face. The upstream Kaggle listing reports
MIT; the HF mirror has no explicit license field. This repository
publishes identifiers, labels, splits and download instructions, not
copies of source product images. See sources/dataset_license_verification.json.

The v3 multi-domain study additionally uses CUB-200-2011 (Wah et al.,
Caltech-UCSD Birds, 2011) and Describable Textures Dataset (Cimpoi et al.,
CVPR 2014). CUB images are restricted to non-commercial research and
education; DTD is provided for research purposes. Image copyrights remain
with their respective owners. No source bird or texture images are
redistributed. Project code/head licensing does not waive dataset terms
or assert commercial-use clearance. See sources/research_datasets_v3.json.

No affiliation with or endorsement by the upstream authors is implied.
